## Result

**Phone agent is live on Freya (published version 2).**
- Workflow id `1d4f5a10-3fe8-4dd5-8f68-894f40dfe984`, agent id `3ab6e8e5-5be0-4fce-96f0-85378568c875` (in `.freya-agents.json`)
- Builder: `build_final.py` (deterministic; `--dry` validates). Export: `submission/final.workflow.json` (35 nodes, 5 global handlers); notes in `submission/README.md`. Tools call the given mock at `https://freya-bank-mock-fable.freya-faruk.workers.dev/voice/v1/*`.

**Design choices that drive accuracy**
- All money/date speech is composed in code nodes, not by the model: Turkish number-to-words (lira/kuruş, sent/peni, zero kuruş dropped), suffix harmony, digit-by-digit last-4, the three TL paid/unpaid cases, Dolar→Euro→İngiliz Sterlini order, the one-sentence no-debt list (missing GBP block excluded), auto-payment remainder, due-date today/passed, statement-day, no-statement-yet, NO_DEBT reading. The reading is spoken as a fixed line, so figures can't drift.
- Card selection: the model only extracts what the caller said; a code node matches name / partial name / last 4 / last 6 / full number, handles "all of them", supplementary cards, duplicates (asks last six, then full number), 3 tries → "Size şu anda yardımcı olamıyorum…".
- Follow-ups per the 8 Oct analysis + 9 Oct corrections: other-card question before the offer; offer only what the caller can use (e-mail dropped when none registered); e-mail read-back + explicit yes, only latest statement, only registered address; week change with preview, joint-statement warning *before* the question, "Olur herhalde" rejected, change made once after a clear "evet"; out-of-scope asks "…ana menüye aktarmamı ister misiniz?"; three calming replies; never more than last-4 digits.
- Global handlers → exact closing lines for agent request, payment, dispute, third-party card, non-Turkish; service failures → agent (week services use the week sentence); `cards.list` 404 → "uygun kart bulunmuyor".

**Verified in simulations** (transcripts in `results_sim.log`, `results_sim2.log`): Example 1 (single card, partial payment, Euro), Example 2/5 (week change, vague answer re-asked, change once with preview dates), Example 3 ("all cards" twice), Example 4 (last month's statement by e-mail) — all judged pass.

**Caveats**
- `/api/v2/chat/message` returns 504 on the first turn (two API calls + code before speaking) — a chat-route limitation; simulations run fine.
- Silence handling and the "statement-week right already used" case can't be detected (no flag in the contract), so the change is always offered, as the sources leave it.

